{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"agent_message","text":"The frozen runner check passed. The operational copy contains the analysis script, report, result maps and figures, while the Git status also shows untracked and ignored worker material; I’m treating all of that as part of the delivery. I’m narrowing the manifest view now so the inspection stays tied to the canonical capture identity and retained file map."}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/bash -lc '\"$STAMPED_ASSESSMENT_PYTHON\" \"$STAMPED_ASSESSMENT_RUNNER\" probes --help\n\"$STAMPED_ASSESSMENT_PYTHON\" \"$STAMPED_ASSESSMENT_RUNNER\" response --help\n\"$STAMPED_ASSESSMENT_PYTHON\" \"$STAMPED_ASSESSMENT_RUNNER\" fresh-rerun --help\npython - <<'\"'PY'\nimport json, os\nfor k in ['STAMPED_DELIVERY_MANIFEST','STAMPED_OPERATIONAL_MANIFEST','STAMPED_WORKER_STOP_RECEIPT','STAMPED_ASSESSMENT_VERSION']:\n p=os.environ[k]; d=json.load(open(p)); print('\\\\n',k, p)\n if 'entries' in d:\n  print('keys',list(d)); print('capture', {x:d.get(x) for x in ['capture_id','capture_sha256','sha256','head','commit','original_head']})\n  print('entry_count',len(d['entries']))\n  print('top-level non-git relevant entries:')\n  for e in d['entries']:\n   path=e.get('path','')\n   if not path.startswith('content/workspace/.git/') and (path.count('/') <= 2 or path.startswith('content/workspace/results/') or path.startswith('content/workspace/input/')):\n    print(e.get('kind'),path,e.get('sha256'),e.get('target'))\n else: print(json.dumps({x:d.get(x) for x in d if x not in ['declared_artifacts','entries']},indent=2))\nPY\nprintf '%s\\\\n' '--- worker-authored files ---'\nfor f in REPORT.md analyze.py input/upstream-methods.md input/participants.tsv input/study-task.md; do echo \\\"### \"'$f\"; sed -n '\"'1,240p' \\\"\"'$STAMPED_JUDGE_TARGET/$f\"; done\nprintf '\"'%s\\\\n' '--- assessment-related frozen input files ---'\nfind \\\"\"'$(dirname \"$STAMPED_ASSESSMENT_VERSION\")\" -maxdepth 2 -type f -print'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/bash -lc '\"$STAMPED_ASSESSMENT_PYTHON\" \"$STAMPED_ASSESSMENT_RUNNER\" probes --help\n\"$STAMPED_ASSESSMENT_PYTHON\" \"$STAMPED_ASSESSMENT_RUNNER\" response --help\n\"$STAMPED_ASSESSMENT_PYTHON\" \"$STAMPED_ASSESSMENT_RUNNER\" fresh-rerun --help\npython - <<'\"'PY'\nimport json, os\nfor k in ['STAMPED_DELIVERY_MANIFEST','STAMPED_OPERATIONAL_MANIFEST','STAMPED_WORKER_STOP_RECEIPT','STAMPED_ASSESSMENT_VERSION']:\n p=os.environ[k]; d=json.load(open(p)); print('\\\\n',k, p)\n if 'entries' in d:\n  print('keys',list(d)); print('capture', {x:d.get(x) for x in ['capture_id','capture_sha256','sha256','head','commit','original_head']})\n  print('entry_count',len(d['entries']))\n  print('top-level non-git relevant entries:')\n  for e in d['entries']:\n   path=e.get('path','')\n   if not path.startswith('content/workspace/.git/') and (path.count('/') <= 2 or path.startswith('content/workspace/results/') or path.startswith('content/workspace/input/')):\n    print(e.get('kind'),path,e.get('sha256'),e.get('target'))\n else: print(json.dumps({x:d.get(x) for x in d if x not in ['declared_artifacts','entries']},indent=2))\nPY\nprintf '%s\\\\n' '--- worker-authored files ---'\nfor f in REPORT.md analyze.py input/upstream-methods.md input/participants.tsv input/study-task.md; do echo \\\"### \"'$f\"; sed -n '\"'1,240p' \\\"\"'$STAMPED_JUDGE_TARGET/$f\"; done\nprintf '\"'%s\\\\n' '--- assessment-related frozen input files ---'\nfind \\\"\"'$(dirname \"$STAMPED_ASSESSMENT_VERSION\")\" -maxdepth 2 -type f -print'","aggregated_output":"✔ The default environment has been installed.\nusage: run_probes.py [-h] [-o OUTPUT] [--response RESPONSE]\n                     [--only {ci-present,clone-weight,derived-have-records,entry-point,env-spec-tracked,inputs-untouched,large-in-annex,license-declared,modules-separated,no-abs-paths,platform-assumptions,run-env-linked,subdatasets-resolvable,tree-clean} [{ci-present,clone-weight,derived-have-records,entry-point,env-spec-tracked,inputs-untouched,large-in-annex,license-declared,modules-separated,no-abs-paths,platform-assumptions,run-env-linked,subdatasets-resolvable,tree-clean} ...]]\n                     [--skip {ci-present,clone-weight,derived-have-records,entry-point,env-spec-tracked,inputs-untouched,large-in-annex,license-declared,modules-separated,no-abs-paths,platform-assumptions,run-env-linked,subdatasets-resolvable,tree-clean} [{ci-present,clone-weight,derived-have-records,entry-point,env-spec-tracked,inputs-untouched,large-in-annex,license-declared,modules-separated,no-abs-paths,platform-assumptions,run-env-linked,subdatasets-resolvable,tree-clean} ...]]\n                     [--check-remote] [--allow GLOB [GLOB ...]]\n                     [--kind {dataset,component,study,skill}] [--overwrite]\n                     [--quiet]\n                     path\n\nRun the STAMPED probes over a checked-out research object.\n\n    run_probes.py <path> [-o probes.json] [--response response.json]\n                  [--only NAME ...] [--skip NAME ...] [--check-remote]\n                  [--kind dataset|component|study|skill]\n\nWrites the per-probe results, and optionally a response JSON (the format in\n``../stamped-conventions/references/response-format.md``) in which every item a\nprobe speaks to carries that probe's verdict and every other item is left\n``not-checked`` for the assessing session to judge.\nWithout a Git commit, ``-o`` retains a limitation receipt and exit code 2;\nno response draft is produced.\n\nThe probes never modify the object.  Nothing here replaces the judgement items:\na response straight out of this script is a draft, not an assessment.\n\npositional arguments:\n  path                  checked-out object to probe\n\noptions:\n  -h, --help            show this help message and exit\n  -o, --output OUTPUT   write the probe results here\n  --response RESPONSE   also write a draft response JSON here\n  --only {ci-present,clone-weight,derived-have-records,entry-point,env-spec-tracked,inputs-untouched,large-in-annex,license-declared,modules-separated,no-abs-paths,platform-assumptions,run-env-linked,subdatasets-resolvable,tree-clean} [{ci-present,clone-weight,derived-have-records,entry-point,env-spec-tracked,inputs-untouched,large-in-annex,license-declared,modules-separated,no-abs-paths,platform-assumptions,run-env-linked,subdatasets-resolvable,tree-clean} ...]\n                        run just these probes\n  --skip {ci-present,clone-weight,derived-have-records,entry-point,env-spec-tracked,inputs-untouched,large-in-annex,license-declared,modules-separated,no-abs-paths,platform-assumptions,run-env-linked,subdatasets-resolvable,tree-clean} [{ci-present,clone-weight,derived-have-records,entry-point,env-spec-tracked,inputs-untouched,large-in-annex,license-declared,modules-separated,no-abs-paths,platform-assumptions,run-env-linked,subdatasets-resolvable,tree-clean} ...]\n  --check-remote        contact submodule urls (network)\n  --allow GLOB [GLOB ...]\n                        paths no-abs-paths may skip, for files that genuinely\n                        have to carry a host path\n  --kind {dataset,component,study,skill}\n  --overwrite           replace an existing --response file instead of keeping\n                        its judged answers\n  --quiet\n✔ The default environment has been installed.\nusage: encode_response.py [-h]\n                          {items,validate,encode,decode,template,set,stamp,table} ...\n\nSTAMPED checklist responses: read the items, validate, encode, decode.\n\nThe vendored checklist in ``../checklist/`` is the only item source, and this\nscript is the only writer of a checklist-app URL.  See\n``../references/response-format.md`` for the response JSON and\n``../references/verdicts.md`` for the statuses.\n\nSubcommands\n-----------\nitems      list the pinned items (id, level, principle codes, text)\nset        answer one item in a response JSON, in place (what every run was\n           otherwise writing a merge script for)\ntable      the per-item markdown table response-format.md section 4 asks for\nstamp      fill harness, model, scope and kind; optionally hash a retained capture\nvalidate   check a response JSON against the pin and the app's constraints\nencode     response JSON -> checklist-app URL\ndecode     checklist-app URL -> response JSON (how a filled web form becomes\n           reference answers for calibration)\ntemplate   emit a response JSON skeleton with every item not-checked\n\nExit codes: 0 ok, 1 validation failed, 2 usage.\n\npositional arguments:\n  {items,validate,encode,decode,template,set,stamp,table}\n    items               list the pinned items\n    validate            check a response JSON\n    encode              response JSON -> URL\n    decode              URL -> response JSON\n    template            emit an all-not-checked response JSON\n    set                 answer one item in a response JSON, in place\n    stamp               fill harness, model, scope, kind and capture identity\n    table               print the per-item markdown table\n\noptions:\n  -h, --help            show this help message and exit\n✔ The default environment has been installed.\nusage: assessment.py [-h] --path PATH --entry ENTRY\n                     --outputs OUTPUTS [OUTPUTS ...] --workdir WORKDIR\n                     -o OUTPUT [--rtol RTOL] [--timeout TIMEOUT]\n                     [--max-get-gb MAX_GET_GB] [--in-container IN_CONTAINER]\n\nReplay documented outputs from a verified complete copy, never from HEAD.\n\noptions:\n  -h, --help            show this help message and exit\n  --path PATH\n  --entry ENTRY\n  --outputs OUTPUTS [OUTPUTS ...]\n  --workdir WORKDIR\n  -o, --output OUTPUT\n  --rtol RTOL\n  --timeout TIMEOUT\n  --max-get-gb MAX_GET_GB\n  --in-container IN_CONTAINER\n\n STAMPED_DELIVERY_MANIFEST /Users/johnlee/.local/state/stamped-in-practice/narps-neutral-v1/a