obe covers this item; a reading of the object is required.\",\n      \"status\": \"not-checked\",\n      \"evidence\": [],\n      \"source\": \"judgement\",\n      \"flags\": []\n    },\n    \"stamped-checklist:should/004\": {\n      \"value\": null,\n      \"reason\": \"No probe covers this item; a reading of the object is required.\",\n      \"status\": \"not-checked\",\n      \"evidence\": [],\n      \"source\": \"judgement\",\n      \"flags\": []\n    },\n    \"stamped-checklist:should/005\": {\n      \"value\": null,\n      \"reason\": \"No probe covers this item; a reading of the object is required.\",\n      \"status\": \"not-checked\",\n      \"evidence\": [],\n      \"source\": \"judgement\",\n      \"flags\": []\n    },\n    \"stamped-checklist:should/006\": {\n      \"value\": null,\n      \"reason\": \"No recognized CI configuration; inspect equivalent environment-reconstitution records.\",\n      \"status\": \"not-checked\",\n      \"evidence\": [\n        {\n          \"uri\": \"probe:ci-present\",\n          \"description\": \"no tracked .github/workflows/, .gitlab-ci.yml, .circleci/, .forgejo/workflows/, .gitea/workflows/ in 58 tracked paths\",\n          \"sha256\": null\n        }\n      ],\n      \"source\": \"probe:ci-present\",\n      \"flags\": []\n    },\n    \"stamped-checklist:should/007\": {\n      \"value\": null,\n      \"reason\": \"No probe covers this item; a reading of the object is required.\",\n      \"status\": \"not-checked\",\n      \"evidence\": [],\n      \"source\": \"judgement\",\n      \"flags\": []\n    },\n    \"stamped-checklist:should/008\": {\n      \"value\": null,\n      \"reason\": \"No probe covers this item; a reading of the object is required.\",\n      \"status\": \"not-checked\",\n      \"evidence\": [],\n      \"source\": \"judgement\",\n      \"flags\": []\n    },\n    \"stamped-checklist:may/001\": {\n      \"value\": null,\n      \"reason\": \"Inspect independently maintained project components; ordinary runtime/package dependencies are environment evidence. No components makes this item N/A.\",\n      \"status\": \"not-checked\",\n      \"evidence\": [],\n      \"source\": \"probe:subdatasets-resolvable\",\n      \"flags\": []\n    },\n    \"stamped-checklist:may/002\": {\n      \"value\": null,\n      \"reason\": \"No probe covers this item; a reading of the object is required.\",\n      \"status\": \"not-checked\",\n      \"evidence\": [],\n      \"source\": \"judgement\",\n      \"flags\": []\n    },\n    \"stamped-checklist:may/003\": {\n      \"value\": null,\n      \"reason\": \"No probe covers this item; a reading of the object is required.\",\n      \"status\": \"not-checked\",\n      \"evidence\": [],\n      \"source\": \"judgement\",\n      \"flags\": []\n    },\n    \"stamped-checklist:may/004\": {\n      \"value\": null,\n      \"reason\": \"No probe covers this item; a reading of the object is required.\",\n      \"status\": \"not-checked\",\n      \"evidence\": [],\n      \"source\": \"judgement\",\n      \"flags\": []\n    },\n    \"stamped-checklist:may/005\": {\n      \"value\": null,\n      \"reason\": \"No probe covers this item; a reading of the object is required.\",\n      \"status\": \"not-checked\",\n      \"evidence\": [],\n      \"source\": \"judgement\",\n      \"flags\": []\n    }\n  },\n  \"schema_version\": \"0.2.0\",\n  \"principles_version\": \"0.2.0\",\n  \"checklist_source\": {\n    \"repo\": \"https://github.com/stamped-principles/stamped-checklist-schema\",\n    \"tag\": \"v0.3.1\",\n    \"commit\": \"af259bad237fa57b856417db8dba45a1b283a527\"\n  },\n  \"extra_items\": [\n    {\n      \"key\": \"clone-weight\",\n      \"status\": \"met\",\n      \"reason\": \"No text blob in git exceeds 10 MiB.\",\n      \"evidence\": [\n        {\n          \"uri\": \"git ls-tree -r -l HEAD\",\n          \"description\": \"largest text blob under 10485760 bytes\",\n          \"sha256\": null\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"key\": \"inputs-untouched\",\n      \"status\": \"not-applicable\",\n      \"reason\": \"N/A: no linked modules, so there is no recorded input state to compare against.\",\n      \"evidence\": []\n    },\n    {\n      \"key\": \"license-declared\",\n      \"status\": \"unmet\",\n      \"reason\": \"No LICENSE, LICENSES/, REUSE.toml or BIDS License field: reuse terms are unstated.\",\n      \"evidence\": [\n        {\n          \"uri\": \"probe:license-declared\",\n          \"description\": \"no licence file among 58 tracked paths, and no License field in any dataset_description.json\",\n          \"sha256\": null\n        }\n      ]\n    }\n  ],\n  \"object\": {\n    \"url\": null,\n    \"commit\": \"8a84ddc3eec68d0b7513f9a15ce37174288b36b7\",\n    \"captured_at\": \"2026-10-16T11:03:37+00:00\",\n    \"kind\": \"study\"\n  },\n  \"assessor\": {\n    \"skill\": \"assess-alignment-with-stamped-principles\",\n    \"version\": \"0.1.0\",\n    \"harness\": null,\n    \"model\": null,\n    \"date\": \"2026-10-16\",\n    \"drafted_by\": \"scripts/run_probes.py\"\n  },\n  \"scope\": \"Probe sweep only; judgement items are left not-checked.\"\n}\nstamped-checklist:must/001\tmust\tS.1\tAre all files and directories nested under a common root?\nstamped-checklist:must/002\tmust\tS.1\tAre datasets included, linked, or referenced reachable from the code and environment specifications without crossing the boundary of a common root?\nstamped-checklist:must/003\tmust\tS.1\tIs external software included in the environment or linked as submodules within the project boundary?\nstamped-checklist:must/004\tmust\tT.1,T.3,T.5\tAre version control systems such as `Git` used for code, text, documentation, and configuration files?\nstamped-checklist:must/005\tmust\tT.1,T.3,T.5\tAre version control systems such as `git-annex`, DataLad, or `Git` LFS used for large binary data?\nstamped-checklist:must/006\tmust\tT.1,T.3,T.5\tAre the exact environment specifications used to generate a set of results included in the provenance records to link computational actions to particular environments?\nstamped-checklist:must/007\tmust\tA.1\tIs a `README.md` or `Makefile` included with instructions for installation and usage?\nstamped-checklist:must/008\tmust\tA.1\tIs there a clear starting point for users to start reproducing results (e.g., a main script, a workflow definition, or a container image)?\nstamped-checklist:must/009\tmust\tP.1\tAre relative paths used in scripts, avoiding hardcoded or system-specific paths like `C:\\Users\\...` or `/home/user/...`?\nstamped-checklist:must/010\tmust\tP.1\tAre all software dependencies included in the environment specification, rather than relying on pre-installed tools?\nstamped-checklist:must/011\tmust\tP.1\tHave all assumptions about the host system's configuration been documented (e.g., specific OS versions, required system libraries, or environment variables)?\nstamped-checklist:must/012\tmust\tP.2\tIs there a clear list of system requirements and dependencies documented in the README or environment specifications?\nstamped-checklist:must/013\tmust\tP.3\tAre environment specifications (e.g., Dockerfiles, `pyproject.toml`, `package.json`) included in the version control system alongside code and data?\nstamped-checklist:must/014\tmust\tP.3\tIs there a process for updating environment specifications when dependencies change, and are these updates tracked in version control?\nstamped-checklist:must/015\tmust\tD.1\tAre environment specifications (e.g., container digests, frozen package manifests) included to ensure others can attempt to exactly replicate the environment?\nstamped-checklist:must/016\tmust\tD.1\tAre environment specifications shared in a way that others can access and use them (e.g., published container images, archived environment files)?\nstamped-checklist:must/017\tmust\tD.1\tIs there documentation on how to obtain and use the environment specifications for reproduction?\nstamped-checklist:should/001\tshould\tT.2\tIs a common version control system (e.g., `Git`, DVC, `git-annex`, or DataLad) used across all components?\nstamped-checklist:should/002\tshould\tA.2\tIs the workflow tested regularly to ensure instructions remain accurate?\nstamped-checklist:should/003\tshould\tM.1\tAre raw data, processed data, code, and environment definitions separated into distinct modules?\nstamped-checklist:should/009\tshould\tM.4\tAre restricted data or software kept in their own modules?\nstamped-checklist:should/004\tshould\tE.1\tIs the pipeline tested in a fresh container, batch job, clean virtual machine, or cloud-based instance?\nstamped-checklist:should/005\tshould\tE.1\tDoes the workflow spawn disposable environments for each execution, allowing for isolation of runs?\nstamped-checklist:should/006\tshould\tD.2\tAre the exact environment specifications used to generate a specific set of results regularly tested to ensure they can be reconstituted as intended?\nstamped-checklist:should/007\tshould\tD.2\tAre environment artifacts archived within the research object where possible (e.g., executable binaries, container images)?\nstamped-checklist:should/008\tshould\tD.2\tIs there a process for updating environment specifications when dependencies change, and are these updates tracked in version control?\nstamped-checklist:may/001\tmay\tM.2\tAre external datasets or software dependencies included as submodules or linked as submodules?\nstamped-checklist:may/002\tmay\tM.2\tIs the modular structure documented to clarify how components relate and can be recombined?\nstamped-checklist:may/003\tmay\tM.2\tAre modular boundaries defined in a way that allows independent updates without breaking the overall workflow?\nstamped-checklist:may/004\tmay\tM.2\tIs there a clear mechanism for composing modules together (e.g., `git` submodules, or container orchestration)?\nstamped-checklist:may/005\tmay\tM.2\tIs there documentation or tooling to support users in understanding and navigating the modular structure?\n✔ The default environment has been installed.\n--- remotes and config ---\n[core]\n\trepositoryformatversion = 0\n\tfilemode = true\n\tbare = false\n\tlogallrefupdates = true\n\tignorecase = true\n\tprecomposeunicode = true\n\thooksPath = /Users/johnlee/.local/state/stamped-in-practice/narps-neutral-v1/workspaces/narps-neutral-r1-22/.git/hooks\n[annex]\n\tuuid = 6f1e3ec2-aada-4036-aadf-5e04b56f3b4e\n\tversion = 10\n[filter \"annex\"]\n\tsmudge = git-annex smudge -- %f\n\tclean = git-annex smudge --clean -- %f\n\tprocess = git-annex filter-process\n--- report line numbers ---\n     1\t# Potential gains and vmPFC activity\n     2\t\n     3\t## Question and conclusion\n     4\t\n     5\tIn the 54-person NARPS equal-indifference group, the supplied gain-effect maps do **not** support a positive gain association in vmPFC under whole-brain family-wise error (FWE) correction. In a bilateral medial orbitofrontal anatomical proxy for vmPFC, the mean participant effect was −0.008 supplied units (95% t interval −0.035 to 0.019); no voxel in that proxy survived whole-brain correction. This is absence of evidence for the predicted positive effect in these maps, not evidence that the true effect is exactly zero.\n     6\t\n     7\tThe whole-brain test did identify 23 positive FWE-significant voxels in three small posterior-inferior foci (peak t=6.62 at MNI [−26, −102, −3.6]; two other peaks are listed in `results/fwe_clusters.tsv`). These do not overlap the vmPFC proxy. They lie near the posterior-inferior edge of the analyzed brain; one peak is outside AAL3-labeled tissue. I therefore do not interpret them as evidence about gain coding or as a vmPFC finding.\n     8\t\n     9\t## Group model and inference\n    10\t\n    11\tI tested whether the unweighted mean of the 54 participant gain-effect estimates was greater than zero at each voxel. The maps are participant contrast parameter estimates, not t/z statistics. Because participant variance maps were not supplied, I used an unweighted one-sample group t statistic rather than precision-weighted second-level inference. A one-sided sign-flip randomization test (5,000 random sign patterns; fixed seed 20261016) evaluated the positive-direction hypothesis. For each randomization, I recorded the maximum t over the analysis mask; voxel p-values are adjusted against that maximum distribution, controlling whole-brain voxelwise FWE at 0.05. The 95th percentile maximum-t threshold was 5.39. Sign flipping assumes independent participants and a symmetric null distribution of participant effects. The original NARPS instructions posed a positive, region-specific hypothesis and required support decisions from whole-brain-corrected analyses; this analysis keeps that whole-brain correction rather than treating an uncorrected ROI result as support ([NARPS analysis instructions](https://www.narps.info/files/narps_instructions_for_analysis_teams.pdf); [permutation inference background](https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC6871862/)).\n    12\t\n    13\tThe analysis mask intersected an MNI152 standard brain mask with voxels nonzero in at least 49 of 54 maps and finite in every map (192,339 voxels). The vmPFC anatomical proxy was the bilateral `Frontal_Med_Orb` parcel in AAL3v2, mapped to the input grid using nearest-neighbor resampling. This is an explicit reproducible anatomical proxy, not a claim that one atlas parcel exhaustively defines functional vmPFC ([AAL3 atlas paper](https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/31521825/)). The ROI summary is descriptive; it does not replace or relax whole-brain correction.\n    14\t\n    15\t## Data checks and limitations\n    16\t\n    17\tAll 54 supplied maps matched the equal-indifference participant IDs, shared the same MNI grid, loaded with finite data, and passed the SHA256 values in the supplied manifest. No participant was excluded. The task’s potential-gain range was twice its potential-loss range, as described in the supplied methods. However, the upstream gain regressor was mean-centered and variance-normalized before HRF convolution, so these coefficients are not change per currency unit. The estimates are conditional on the upstream choice to model gain separately from loss and on its other fixed first-level terms. This group analysis cannot revisit those modeling decisions.\n    18\t\n    19\tThe lack of participant variance maps prevents a precision-weighted mixed-effects analysis and limits uncertainty modeling to variation across the supplied participant estimates. The permutation result relies on sign-flip symmetry. AAL3 medial orbitofrontal cortex is an imperfect vmPFC proxy, and the maps’ MNI152NLin2009cAsym space and the standard mask/atlas are not identical templates. The interval around the proxy mean includes zero and is not an equivalence interval: modest positive or spatially heterogeneous effects remain possible. A non-significant whole-brain-corrected result therefore means this group analysis did not establish a positive vmPFC effect at the chosen error rate; it does not show that increasing gains have no neural correlate. More broadly, the parametric map association does not establish that potential gain causally produces a response.\n    20\t\n    21\t## Figures\n    22\t\n    23\t**Figure 1.** Participant-average effect within bilateral medial orbitofrontal vmPFC proxy. Each dot is one participant; the diamond and interval show the mean and descriptive 95% t interval across participants.\n    24\t\n    25\t![Participant effects in vmPFC proxy](results/vmPFC_proxy_effects.png)\n    26\t\n    27\t**Figure 2.** Positive t statistics exceeding the 95th percentile of the whole-brain maximum-t null distribution; green outline is the vmPFC proxy. Small corrected foci occur posterior-inferior to the proxy and are not interpreted anatomically.\n    28\t\n    29\t![Whole-brain corrected map](results/wholebrain_fwe_map.png)\n    30\t\n    31\t## Reproducibility files\n    32\t\n    33\t- `analyze.py` — complete group-analysis and figure-generation script (Python with NumPy, pandas, SciPy, NiBabel, Nilearn, and Matplotlib).\n    34\t- `results/summary.json` — numeric analysis summary and QC decisions.\n    35\t- `results/fwe_clusters.tsv` — descriptive extents and peak coordinates for corrected voxels; cluster extent itself was not the inferential correction.\n    36\t- `results/participant_qc.tsv` — per-participant coverage and effect summaries.\n    37\t- `results/group_mask.nii.gz`, `results/mean_effect.nii.gz`, `results/t_statistic.nii.gz`, `results/p_fwe_maxT.nii.gz` — analysis mask, mean, t, and max-T adjusted p maps.\n    38\t- `results/vmPFC_proxy_aal3.nii.gz` — resampled anatomical proxy used for localization.\n    39\t\n    40\tReproduce from the workspace root with:\n    41\t\n    42\t```bash\n    43\t/Users/johnlee/.local/state/stamped-in-practice/narps-neutral-v1/common-environment/.pixi/envs/default/bin/python analyze.py\n    44\t```\n--- worker receipt key summary ---\nreceipt_sha cac1a272faf44f4e459f21af394256880b4c98e91e94a44b6939cc92cba45c83\nworker {'pid': 59608, 'returncode': 0, 'stop_reason': 'exited', 'stopped_at': '2026-10-16T06:59:04.511404+00:00', 'timed_out': False}\nartifacts\ninventory entries 0\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
