{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_20","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/bash -lc \"python - <<'PY'\nimport os\np=os.path.join(os.environ['STAMPED_JUDGE_OUTPUT'],'assessment-report.md')\ns=open(p).read().replace('2 not-checked / 1 not-applicable (10 items)','2 not-checked / 1 not-applicable (9 items)').replace('1 met / 1 partial / 2 unmet / 0 not-checked / 2 not-applicable (6 items)','1 met / 1 partial / 1 unmet / 0 not-checked / 2 not-applicable (5 items)')\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nPY\n\\\"\"'$STAMPED_ASSESSMENT_PYTHON\" \"$STAMPED_ASSESSMENT_RUNNER\" response encode --help\n\"$STAMPED_ASSESSMENT_PYTHON\" \"$STAMPED_ASSESSMENT_RUNNER\" validate --help\ncat response.json | head -80\nnl -ba assessment-report.md | head -25'","aggregated_output":"✔ The default environment has been installed.\nusage: encode_response.py encode [-h] [--base-url BASE_URL] [--allow-invalid]\n                                 response\n\npositional arguments:\n  response\n\noptions:\n  -h, --help           show this help message and exit\n  --base-url BASE_URL\n  --allow-invalid      encode even if validation fails\n✔ The default environment has been installed.\nusage: encode_response.py validate [-h] response\n\npositional arguments:\n  response\n\noptions:\n  -h, --help  show this help message and exit\n{\n  \"checklist_version\": \"0.3.1\",\n  \"responses\": {\n    \"stamped-checklist:must/001\": {\n      \"reason\": \"All captured workspace content is under the workspace root.\",\n      \"status\": \"met\",\n      \"evidence\": [\n        {\n          \"uri\": \"capture://62844be8e123ee4970d90409a641082a3126743ee3b90d914b2b5ef26a50aaf1/content/workspace/REPORT.md\",\n          \"description\": \"Worker report at stop state; original capture SHA-256 62844be8e123ee4970d90409a641082a3126743ee3b90d914b2b5ef26a50aaf1\",\n          \"sha256\": \"87a86bc213b9e8157957666a1263c32249e4ff4ae5d2a677a115aaf89c743248\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"source\": \"judgement\",\n      \"flags\": []\n    },\n    \"stamped-checklist:must/002\": {\n      \"reason\": \"All 54 input-map links resolve within the captured workspace to retained annex objects.\",\n      \"status\": \"met\",\n      \"evidence\": [\n        {\n          \"uri\": \"capture://62844be8e123ee4970d90409a641082a3126743ee3b90d914b2b5ef26a50aaf1/content/workspace/input/data/\",\n          \"description\": \"Participant-map links are internal workspace paths; the complete capture retains their annex content.\",\n          \"sha256\": null\n        },\n        {\n          \"uri\": \"capture://62844be8e123ee4970d90409a641082a3126743ee3b90d914b2b5ef26a50aaf1/content/workspace/.git/annex/objects/\",\n          \"description\": \"Retained annex object bytes are inside the common root.\",\n          \"sha256\": null\n        }\n      ],\n      \"source\": \"judgement\",\n      \"flags\": []\n    },\n    \"stamped-checklist:must/003\": {\n      \"reason\": \"No delivered environment specification or vendored external software dependencies are present.\",\n      \"status\": \"unmet\",\n      \"evidence\": [\n        {\n          \"uri\": \"capture://62844be8e123ee4970d90409a641082a3126743ee3b90d914b2b5ef26a50aaf1/content/workspace/REPORT.md\",\n          \"description\": \"Worker report at stop state; original capture SHA-256 62844be8e123ee4970d90409a641082a3126743ee3b90d914b2b5ef26a50aaf1\",\n          \"sha256\": \"87a86bc213b9e8157957666a1263c32249e4ff4ae5d2a677a115aaf89c743248\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"uri\": \"probes.json\",\n          \"description\": \"Frozen runner probe output; saved assessment artifact\",\n          \"sha256\": \"3b236dd3900c227beba5a721a730a95ee5c70a8d56741006794ca61de73c3cc4\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"source\": \"judgement\",\n      \"flags\": []\n    },\n    \"stamped-checklist:must/004\": {\n      \"reason\": \"Git is used, but the report, analysis, cache and results were untracked at worker stop.\",\n      \"status\": \"unmet\",\n      \"evidence\": [\n        {\n          \"uri\": \"git status --short --ignored (operational copy)\",\n          \"description\": \"Probe observed ?? REPORT.md, ?? analyze.py, ?? atlas_cache/, ?? results/; worker stop receipt records the same stop state.\",\n          \"sha256\": null\n        },\n        {\n          \"uri\": \"/Users/johnlee/.local/state/stamped-in-practice/narps-neutral-v1/assessment-series/narps-neutral-r1-operational-v4/judgments/narps-neutral-r1-22-j01/attempt-01/worker-end-state.json\",\n          \"description\": \"Worker stop receipt; SHA-256 cac1a272faf44f4e459f21af394256880b4c98e91e94a44b6939cc92cba45c83\",\n          \"sha256\": \"cac1a272faf44f4e459f21af394256880b4c98e91e94a44b6939cc92cba45c83\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"uri\": \"probes.json\",\n          \"description\": \"Frozen runner probe output; saved assessment artifact\",\n          \"sha256\": \"3b236dd3900c227beba5a721a730a95ee5c70a8d56741006794ca61de73c3cc4\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"source\": \"judgement\",\n      \"flags\": []\n    },\n    \"stamped-checklist:must/005\": {\n      \"reason\": \"The 54 large participant maps are tracked as annex pointers with retained annex content.\",\n      \"status\": \"met\",\n      \"evidence\": [\n        {\n     1\t# Independent assessment: NARPS Hypothesis 1\n     2\t\n     3\t**STAMPED MUST:** 4 met / 0 partial / 13 unmet / 0 not-checked (17 items). **SHOULD:** 1 met / 2 partial / 4 unmet / 2 not-checked / 1 not-applicable (9 items). **MAY:** 1 met / 1 partial / 1 unmet / 0 not-checked / 2 not-applicable (5 items). These are item findings, not an overall score.\n     4\t\n     5\t## Scientific assessment\n     6\t\n     7\t**Scientific adequacy: supported.** The reported conclusion is well supported as a statement that this analysis did not establish a positive vmPFC gain effect. It uses the complete 54-person equal-indifference cohort, performs whole-brain maximum-T FWE correction, names a reproducible bilateral medial orbitofrontal proxy, and separates descriptive ROI uncertainty from corrected inference. The reported mean in that proxy is −0.008 supplied units (95% t interval −0.035 to 0.019), with no corrected voxels in the proxy. It correctly describes the interval as non-equivalence evidence and avoids inferring absence of any neural association. All ten selected outputs were recreated byte-for-byte in the single replay (see `replay/replay-result.json`).\n     8\t\n     9\t**Reported hypothesis outcome (verbatim):** “In the 54-person NARPS equal-indifference group, the supplied gain-effect maps do **not** support a positive gain association in vmPFC under whole-brain family-wise error (FWE) correction.” [Original capture `content/workspace/REPORT.md`, SHA-256 `87a86bc213b9e8157957666a1263c32249e4ff4ae5d2a677a115aaf89c743248`.] Numeric support: `content/workspace/results/summary.json` reports n=54, 192,339 analysis voxels, 23 corrected voxels outside the proxy, vmPFC proxy mean −0.00795, descriptive 95% t interval [−0.03455, 0.01864], and 0 corrected proxy voxels (SHA-256 `a49299fd75aa0baa130921e207d3e14aa5ca0dd3e7063e2d31203e45219d5e06`).\n    10\t\n    11\tThe model is appropriate for independent participant-level effects when variance maps are unavailable. Sign-flip symmetry is an explicit assumption; the mask, finite/nonzero coverage rule and common image geometry are inspectable in `content/workspace/analyze.py` (SHA-256 `abb28e87b1d03c0d7bcd8effac1bb9afa785fe5004a44ff7e31d017e91790dac`). The report appropriately treats AAL3 medial orbitofrontal cortex as a proxy, notes template differences and gain regressor scaling, and does not interpret posterior-inferior corrected foci as vmPFC. A limitation is that the reported t interval is descriptive and not a whole-brain or equivalence interval; its role is clearly labeled. No material inference error was identified.\n    12\t\n    13\t## Delivery, attribution and scope\n    14\t\n    15\tThe canonical original capture is SHA-256 `62844be8e123ee4970d90409a641082a3126743ee3b90d914b2b5ef26a50aaf1`; the original captured HEAD is `8a84ddc3eec68d0b7513f9a15ce37174288b36b7`. Primary file citations in this report are relative to that captured workspace and name each file's capture SHA-256. The complete capture has 1,209 entries, no declared omissions or capture errors, and preserves ignored files, workspace Git metadata, annex objects and links. The worker-stop receipt (`worker-end-state.json`, SHA-256 `cac1a272faf44f4e459f21af394256880b4c98e91e94a44b6939cc92cba45c83`) records normal worker exit and that the submitted script, report, cache and results were untracked at stop. The scientific artifacts are assessed as supplied; they were not reconstructed from HEAD. Coordinator preservation does not earn worker credit.\n    16\t\n    17\t**Replay declaration and result.** Before replay, the declared entrypoint was `/Users/johnlee/.local/state/stamped-in-practice/narps-neutral-v1/common-environment/.pixi/envs/default/bin/python analyze.py`, as written in the report. Prerequisites were the captured source, the named interpreter and available Python packages, and the supplied atlas cache; no source repair or environment additions were made. Only the ten generated files listed in `replay-plan.json` were selected for removal and comparison; inputs, participant metadata and source code were protected. The frozen helper made a separate complete-delivery copy from the canonical capture, imposed its 7,200-second limit, and performed no input prefetch. All ten outputs were identical; there were no numerical or geometry differences. The helper's return code was 0 and elapsed time was 10.96 seconds. There was no assessor malfunction.\n    18\t\n    19\t**Integrity observation.** The runner's final replay record reports no capture issues. The operational-copy manifest was also compared to the initial operational manifest; any annex keys database metadata change is reported separately in `integrity-check.json`. The operational copy is an observation surface, not worker evidence. No source repair was performed.\n    20\t\n    21\t**Access.** No worker-declared repository, archive, URL or other authorized retrieval route was identified in the report or Git remote configuration. Therefore no intended recipient route, artifact-coverage test or host-scope test could be established. The coordinator-provided copy is not evidence of worker publication. No access route was tested.\n    22\t\n    23\t**Exposure.** No assistance-related identifier was used as grading evidence. The report's external scholarly citations were considered only as cited scientific context.\n    24\t\n    25\t## STAMPED checklist findings\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
