{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_24","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/bash -lc '\"$STAMPED_ASSESSMENT_PYTHON\" \"$STAMPED_ASSESSMENT_RUNNER\" response encode response.json > checklist-link.txt 2> checklist-encode.stderr\ncat > access-record.json <<'\"'JSON'\n{\n  \\\"schema_version\\\": 1,\n  \\\"capture_sha256\\\": \\\"62844be8e123ee4970d90409a641082a3126743ee3b90d914b2b5ef26a50aaf1\\\",\n  \\\"intended_recipient\\\": \\\"A researcher using the worker-declared authorized retrieval route\\\",\n  \\\"worker_declared_route\\\": null,\n  \\\"route_identification\\\": \\\"No worker-declared route was found in the stop-state report or Git remote configuration.\\\",\n  \\\"required_artifact_coverage\\\": [\\\"analysis code\\\", \\\"participant maps\\\", \\\"cohort metadata\\\", \\\"documented environment/dependencies\\\", \\\"reported results and figures\\\"],\n  \\\"tested_artifact_coverage\\\": null,\n  \\\"tested_host_scope\\\": null,\n  \\\"test_status\\\": \\\"not-tested-no-route\\\",\n  \\\"limitation\\\": \\\"Coordinator delivery of the capture does not establish worker publication or access. Anonymous access was not required and was not tested.\\\"\n}\nJSON\ncat >> assessment-report.md <<'MD'\n\n### Individual checklist findings\n\nThe following table is generated from the validated response record; citations use canonical capture SHA-256 \"'`62844be8e123ee4970d90409a641082a3126743ee3b90d914b2b5ef26a50aaf1` and capture-relative paths unless identified as assessment artifacts.\n\nMD\ncat item-table.md >> assessment-report.md\ncat >> assessment-report.md <<'\"'MD'\n\n### Flags, unavailable measures and project kind\n\nFlagged items: \"'`must/007`, `must/008`, and `must/009`. The entry-point probe looks for tracked README/Makefile/workflow files and therefore missed the untracked report'\"'s command (\"'`must/008` met); for `must/007`, the report still omits installation instructions; and the tracked-text absolute-path probe missed the report'\"'s untracked absolute interpreter path (\"'`must/009` unmet). Each judgment is tied to the worker stop state.\n\nNot checked: `should/002` (equivalent repeated workflow-test history was not independently established) and `should/006` (equivalent repeated environment-reconstitution history was not independently established). Worker run-history evidence would settle both. The intended access route was absent, so access and host-scope availability are recorded separately in `access-record.json`.\n\nThe delivery is a computational study/group-analysis project. Its stated goal comes from the retained brief and `content/workspace/input/study-task.md`: analyze the 54 supplied participant gain-effect maps for a positive gain association in vmPFC in the equal-indifference group. The assessment scope is the complete stopped delivery, including untracked and ignored files, plus a single documented replay.\n\nChecklist URL: [checklist-link.txt](checklist-link.txt). The complete response is [response.json](response.json); machine-readable scientific judgment is [scientific-judgment.json](scientific-judgment.json). Probe output: [probes.json](probes.json). Replay output: [replay/replay-result.json](replay/replay-result.json).\n\nProduced by `assess-alignment-with-stamped-principles` 0.1.0 with `stamped-conventions` 0.1.0, checklist 0.3.1 (`stamped-checklist-schema@v0.3.1`, `af259ba`), on the canonical capture at commit `8a84ddc3eec68d0b7513f9a15ce37174288b36b7`, 2026-10-16, Codex API/GPT-6. Canonical capture manifest: `targets/narps-neutral-r1-22-j01/canonical/manifest.json`, SHA-256 `62844be8e123ee4970d90409a641082a3126743ee3b90d914b2b5ef26a50aaf1`. Probe output: `probes.json`.\nMD\npython - <<'\"'PY'\nimport os,json,hashlib\nfrom pathlib import Path\nout=Path(os.environ['STAMPED_JUDGE_OUTPUT'])\nreport=out/'assessment-report.md'; j=out/'scientific-judgment.json'\nd=json.loads(j.read_text()); d['report']['sha256']=hashlib.sha256(report.read_bytes()).hexdigest(); j.writ